The Baggage Rules 2012 specify that any baggage containing the items listed in **Schedule‑2 (Tafsil‑2)** is subject to a **fixed duty or tax** (the amount for each item is set in the schedule). These items include, for example:

* Televisions (Plasma, LCD, TFT, LED) of all sizes (22‑52 inches and larger) – with duties ranging from ৳15,000 to ৳100,000;  
* Home‑theatre / music‑centre systems with more than 4 speakers;  
* Refrigerators / deep‑freezers;  
* Air‑coolers and air‑conditioners (window type and split types up to and above 18,000 BTU);  
* Dish antennas;  
* Gold bars or ingots (up to 200 g) – charged ৳150 per 11.664 g;  
* Silver bars or ingots (up to 200 g) – charged ৳6 per 11.664 g;  
* HD, DV, BETA or professional‑use cameras;  
* Air‑guns / air‑rifles (subject to Ministry of Commerce approval);  
* Lamps (₹300 per unit);  
* Carpet (up to 15 m² – ₹300 per m²);  
* Dish‑washers, washing machines or clothes‑dryers (₹3,000 each).  

Any baggage containing these categories must pay the prescribed fixed duties/taxes; all other personal or household items not listed in Schedule‑2 are duty‑free under the Rules.

In its error‑reporting notice (Form‑ত, বিধি ১৩(৭)), the AEO must:

* give a concise description of the error that occurred;  
* state whether the error led to any customs‑tax evasion or under‑payment;  
* indicate if the error was intentional, unintentional or caused by negligence; and  
* outline the corrective actions or measures taken to prevent the same error from happening again.

The renewal application must be accompanied by the following documents:  

1. A copy of the original (ম‑ল) license;  
2. A copy of the updated trade licence;  
3. A copy of the updated income‑tax certificate;  
4. A copy of the performance certificate for the preceding period;  
5. A copy of the updated office‑rent agreement together with the rent‑payment receipt;  
6. A copy of the renewal‑fee receipt (and any applicable tax receipt); and  
7. The certificate of membership in the relevant C&F association.

To have the newly‑installed machinery entered into the existing warehouse licence, the Deputy or Assistant Commissioner must receive the complete import‑/purchase packet, namely:

* the Bill of Entry (or B/E), the Letter of Credit, the commercial invoice and the Bill of Lading/Air‑way Bill or truck receipt;  
* any import‑permit (IP) issued by BEPZA or BEZA and, where applicable, a copy of the duty (মূসক) invoice;  
* a formal declaration of machine installation and the machine catalogue; and  
* for used or locally‑purchased equipment, a “life‑span” certificate from an internationally recognised surveyor confirming at least ten years of remaining service.  

Submitting these documents together satisfies the requirements for adding the machinery to the licence.

